The obvious “output a Hamilton cycle” family has two immediate risks: for fixed \(n\) every seed is the same instance up to coordinate relabelling, and the witness has \(\Theta(\binom{2n+1}{n})\) entries. I’m checking the paper’s intermediate path systems now; an endpoint/reconstruction problem may preserve its native combinatorics while keeping the witness short.
